  <prompt>
    Write the round-trip agreement test that proves the read-side numbering computation (031) equals the write-side
    numbering author (`ComposeDocumentRenderer`) (design §4 WS-3 "Reference authoring parity"; spec FR-15). Author a
    document via `ComposeDocumentRenderer` — which writes the `%N.` style-linked cascade + `w:start` into
    `numbering.xml` (`LevelText`/`StartNumberingValue`) — then read it back via the WS-3 computation and assert
    IDENTICAL labels. The read-side and write-side numbering models MUST agree; any divergence means the two models
    have forked and must be reconciled before this passes. This is an ADR-038 seam / KEEP-path vertical slice.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer writing an integration/seam test spanning both numbering models. Expert in the
    write-side renderer (`ComposeDocumentRenderer` `LevelText`/`StartNumberingValue`/`ParagraphStyleIdInLevel`) and
    the read-side computation (031). Understands ADR-038's KEEP-path seam model (real components, no `Mock&lt;...&gt;`,
    no DI-registration/ctor-null tests) and that a round-trip is the strongest guarantee the two models agree.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A round-trip seam test: author a doc (with numbered clauses incl. multi-level + style-linked cascade) via
    `ComposeDocumentRenderer` → read it via the WS-3 computation engine → assert the computed labels are identical
    to what the renderer authored. Living at an ADR-038 KEEP path, it fails loudly if the read-side and write-side
    numbering models diverge, and passes only when they agree (FR-15).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      `ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs` is the born-in-editor WRITE path — it already authors a `%N.` style-linked
      cascade + `w:start` into `numbering.xml` (`LevelText` `:574`/`:609`, `StartNumberingValue` `:572`/`:607`,
      `ParagraphStyleIdInLevel` `:586`). WS-3 (030/031) is the READ-side computation of the same model. Design §4
      WS-3 requires the two to agree, proven by a round-trip: author → read → identical labels. This test is that
      proof and the numbering-exactness regression net going forward. Because it spans two real `Services/Compose/`
      components with no mocks, it is an ADR-038 seam vertical slice — the DoD category for dispatch/projection
      changes.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/ (or the established seam path — RE-GREP) — the round-trip numbering-agreement seam test (author via renderer → read via computation → assert identical labels).</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs — the write-side author (`LevelText`/`StartNumberingValue`/`ParagraphStyleIdInLevel`); the test drives this to produce the doc + expected labels.</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs — the WS-3 read-side computation (030/031) under test.</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/spec.md — FR-15 (read-side agrees with write-side mirror; round-trip test), NFR-02 (numbering-exact release blocker), NFR-06 (determinism).</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/design.md §4 WS-3 "Reference authoring parity".</file>
      <file role="adr">docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md — seam / KEEP-path vertical slice; banned mock/DI/ctor tests.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="031" status="pending">Provides the read-side computation engine the round-trip reads with.</dependency>
      <dependency task="032" status="pending">Render complete — the WS-3 numbering is fully wired before the agreement test runs.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-15">The test MUST author via `ComposeDocumentRenderer` and read via the WS-3 computation, asserting IDENTICAL labels. Scope: cover multi-level + style-linked cascades (the constructs the renderer authors); the read-side and write-side numbering models MUST agree.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">The test is a seam / KEEP-path vertical slice over the real renderer + real builder. Scope: NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration test, NO ctor-null test — drive the actual components end-to-end.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / determinism">The round-trip MUST be deterministic (NFR-06). Scope: identical author input → identical read labels across runs; no reliance on render order.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / ADR-013">The test exercises pure `Services/Compose/` code (`byte[]`/OOXML in, projection out). Scope: no `Microsoft.Graph`, no AI-internal type in the test path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / BFF Hygiene §10">No runtime package added. Scope: `dotnet publish -c Release` unaffected — report size + diff vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expect 0); `/conflict-check` before PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Round-trip numbering agreement (write-side renderer ↔ read-side computation); ADR-038 seam / KEEP-path vertical slice; determinism</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/design.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Author → read → assert identical" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs (:570-640)">
        Drive the renderer to author a doc with a known numbered cascade (it writes `%N.` `LevelText` + `StartNumberingValue` + style-linking). Feed the resulting bytes to the WS-3 computation and assert each paragraph's computed label equals the label the renderer's cascade produces. Divergence = the two models forked.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (🔒 RIGOR LEVEL: FULL / 📋 REASON: test-modifying `tests/**` → TEST-MODIFYING override → Step 9.5 unconditional / 📖 PROTOCOL STEPS). Load spec FR-15 + NFR-02/06 + design §4 WS-3 parity + ADR-038.</step>
    <step order="1" name="RE-GREP both sides + the seam path">Confirm `ComposeDocumentRenderer` authoring surface (`LevelText`/`StartNumberingValue`/`ParagraphStyleIdInLevel`) and the established `tests/integration/seam/` path.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Author a doc via the renderer">Drive `ComposeDocumentRenderer` to author a doc with a known numbered cascade (multi-level + style-linked), capturing the expected labels the cascade produces.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Read via the WS-3 computation">Feed the authored bytes through the WS-3 computation (031) and collect the computed labels per paragraph.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Assert identical + determinism">Assert computed labels == authored labels for every paragraph; assert the round-trip is deterministic across repeated runs.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Build + publish check">`dotnet test` the seam suite green; `dotnet publish -c Release` size + diff (0). `/conflict-check` before PR.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Close out">Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set task 033 to ✅. Record any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If write-side (`ComposeDocumentRenderer`) and read-side (WS-3 computation) disagree on ANY label — STOP. The two numbering models have diverged; surface WHICH side is wrong (with the specific construct + expected vs actual) and reconcile before patching the test to pass. Do NOT weaken the assertion to make the round-trip green — that would hide a real numbering-exactness (NFR-02) defect.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run the seam test suite; `dotnet publish -c Release` for the size check.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/ — round-trip numbering-agreement seam test (author via renderer → read via computation → identical labels)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a doc authored via `ComposeDocumentRenderer` with a multi-level + style-linked cascade, when read via the WS-3 computation, then every paragraph's computed label equals the label the renderer's cascade authored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The round-trip is deterministic — repeated runs produce identical labels (NFR-06).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test is an ADR-038 seam / KEEP-path slice over the real renderer + real builder — no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration test, no ctor-null test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if read-side and write-side disagree on any label, the test FAILS loudly (and the escalation fires) — the assertion is not weakened to pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet test` seam suite green; publish size unchanged vs ~49.63 MB baseline; `/conflict-check` clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">TASK-INDEX.md shows task 033 as ✅ and any deviation is recorded in projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Closes the WS-3 numbering slice before deploy (034). This round-trip is the standing regression net that the
    read-side and write-side numbering models stay in agreement — important because R5 G3 will build edit-side
    renumber on 031's engine and must not fork it. TASK-INDEX.md + current-task.md are owned by the main session.
  </notes>

